% Lesson 1 — runnable answers (exercises 1 and 2).
%   python3 datalog.py exercises/01-answers.dl

parent(abe, bob).
parent(abe, ann).
parent(bob, carl).
parent(ann, dana).

sibling(X, Y) :- parent(P, X), parent(P, Y).

% Exercise 1: cousins = children of siblings.  And yes, it inherits the
% sibling bug twice over: everyone with a grandparent is their own
% cousin (via sibling(P, P)), and siblings are each other's cousins.
cousin(X, Y) :- parent(PX, X), parent(PY, Y), sibling(PX, PY).

% Exercise 2: aunt_or_uncle = a sibling of a parent.  Without a
% disequality built-in we cannot exclude the parent themselves, so every
% parent with a sibling-set (including themselves!) appears — the same
% root cause, honestly surfaced.
aunt_or_uncle(A, N) :- parent(P, N), sibling(P, A).
